Explanation:

Local Machine:
You run kubectl, helm, and optionally Scoop/Chocolatey-managed binaries.
PowerShell/Bash is your main CLI.
Minikube VM (Docker Driver):
Kubernetes cluster runs inside a Minikube-managed Docker container.
Pods, Services, Secrets, and Helm-managed applications run here.
Kubernetes Components:
Grafana Pod (monitoring-grafana): Exposes dashboard, stores admin password as Kubernetes Secret.
Prometheus Pod: Handles monitoring metrics.
Helm: Deploys charts and manages configuration of Prometheus/Grafana.
Secrets Handling:
kubectl get secret ... | base64 --decode is used to retrieve sensitive information.
Windows may need coreutils via Scoop to access Linux-like commands (base64, wc, uniq).
2️⃣ Important Notes / Details
Component	Notes / Issues	Recommendations
Minikube Service	Docker driver blocks terminal	Use kubectl port-forward or new terminal
Chocolatey	Temp folder issues, partial install	Remove temp folders, reinstall as Admin
Scoop	Bucket confusion, network timeout	Remove & add buckets, ensure 7-Zip installed
Helm	CLI not found until PATH updated	Add $HOME/scoop/shims to PATH
coreutils	Commands missing (base64, wc, etc.)	Update PATH to $HOME/scoop/apps/coreutils/current/bin
Grafana Secret	Base64 decoding required	Use Linux base64 --decode or PowerShell conversion


